# ArchLucid navigation (quick map)

## Read first

- **Coding agents (repo-level)**: **`docs/engineering/AGENTS.md`** (repo-root **`AGENTS.md`** is a short pointer); **`*.slnf`** partial solution loads + assessments pointers; **`archlucid-ui/AGENTS.md`** for the Next.js app only.
- **archlucid-ui Cursor rules**: `.cursor/rules/UI-React-Next-Conventions.mdc`, `.cursor/rules/UI-Stable-Selectors-And-Snapshots.mdc`, `.cursor/rules/UI-Accessibility-Baseline.mdc`.
- **AI / agent boundaries & prompts**: `.cursor/rules/AI-Agent-Boundaries.mdc` (DTF host-only, orchestrator port, extension seams), `.cursor/rules/AI-Prompt-And-Redaction-Hygiene.mdc` (LLM prompts, redaction, model-call hygiene).
- **LLM-driven assessments (narrow read surface)**: `docs/library/ASSESSMENT_INPUTS.md` then `.cursor/rules/Assessment-Read-First.mdc` (when producing a readiness pass — output to `docs/assessments/LATEST.md`; snapshots in `docs/archive/assessments/`).
- **Weighted readiness assessments (SOC 2 scoring boundary)**: **`@Assessment-Scope-V1_1`** (`.cursor/rules/Assessment-Scope-V1_1.mdc` — not always injected; attach for assessment passes), plus `docs/library/V1_DEFERRED.md` §6c — **`(A)` headline vs `(B)` procurement realism**.
- **Canonical buyer / operator spine**: `docs/START_HERE.md` (decision tree + journey; `docs/FIRST_5_DOCS.md` is a thin redirect).
- **Persona workflow recipes (API / CLI / UI map)**: `docs/library/customer-facing/WORKFLOW_RECIPES_BY_PERSONA.md` (stub at `library/WORKFLOW_RECIPES_BY_PERSONA.md`).
- **Contributor decision tree (what folder to open first)**: `docs/START_HERE.md` — use the persona table + links into the five-document spine.
- **System flows (Mermaid)**: `docs/library/SYSTEM_MAP.md`
- **Component detail**: `docs/library/ARCHITECTURE_COMPONENTS.md`
- **API contracts**: `docs/library/API_CONTRACTS.md`

## Entry points

| Task | Start here |
|------|------------|
| Add a **finding engine** | `ArchLucid.Decisioning/Interfaces/IFindingEngine.cs` → register in `ServiceCollectionExtensions.Decisioning.cs` → template `templates/archlucid-finding-engine/` |
| Add a **context connector** | `ArchLucid.ContextIngestion/Interfaces/IContextConnector.cs`, typed stages (`IConnectorInput<T>` / `IConnectorNormalizer<T>`), pipeline slots (`IConnectorDescriptor` / `ContextConnectorPipeline.CreateOrderedConnectorDescriptors`), orchestrator (`IConnectorPipelineOrchestrator` / `DefaultConnectorPipelineOrchestrator`) → `RegisterContextIngestionAndKnowledgeGraph` (Api startup) |
| Add an **agent handler** | `ArchLucid.AgentRuntime/IAgentHandler.cs` → `RegisterAgentExecution` in `ServiceCollectionExtensions.AgentsGovernanceRetrieval.cs` |
| Add an **alert delivery channel** | `ArchLucid.Decisioning/Alerts/Delivery/IAlertDeliveryChannel.cs` → register with alert dispatcher |
| Change **authority pipeline** | `ArchLucid.Persistence/Orchestration/AuthorityRunOrchestrator.cs` and `Orchestration/Pipeline/*` stages |
| **SQL + RLS + replica** | `ArchLucid.Persistence/Connections/SqlServerOptions.cs` (section `SqlServer`) |
| **Configuration validation** | `ArchLucid.Host.Core/Startup/Validation/ArchLucidConfigurationRules.cs` |

## Data vs persistence

- **`ArchLucid.Persistence.Data.*`**: Dapper repositories against SQL, connection factories, migrations scripts consumption.
- **`ArchLucid.Persistence`**: Domain-oriented persistence ports (`IRunRepository`, UoW, orchestration, caching decorators, archival).

## Product rename (in progress)

- **Brownfield rename / Terraform `state mv`**: `docs/library/V1_DEFERRED.md` §3 and `docs/runbooks/TERRAFORM_STATE_MV_PHASE_7_5.md` — ArchiForge → ArchLucid, done incrementally per `.cursor/rules/Navigation.mdc` (Product rename section).

## Host roles

- **`Hosting:Role`**: `Combined` (default dev), `Api` (HTTP only), `Worker` (background services). See `ArchLucid.Host.Core/Hosting/ArchLucidHostingRole.cs`.
